From: Harry Yoo <harry.yoo@oracle.com>
Subject: x86/mm: drop unnecessary calls to sync_global_pgds() and fold into its sole user
Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2025 10:21:06 +0900

Now that p*d_populate_kernel{,init}() handles page table synchronization,
calling sync_global_pgds() is no longer necessary.  Remove those redundant
calls.

Additionally, since arch_sync_kernel_mappings() is now the only remaining
caller of sync_global_pgds(), fold the function into its user.

Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20250725012106.5316-6-harry.yoo@oracle.com
Signed-off-by: Harry Yoo <harry.yoo@oracle.com>
Suggested-by: Dave Hansen <dave.hansen@linux.intel.com>
